From 83f6b280dddf4cdbd8644a5056ab8fe96df5c561 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <dev@infoverify.local>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 17:30:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix Phone Number Verification page + add slip type tiles
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Root cause: PhoneMultiplePage (/phone) called POST
/verification/nin/phone-multiple against a NIN_PHONE_MULTIPLE service
key - neither ever existed in maria_backend or in Techhub's API, so the
price permanently showed 'Price loading…' and every submit would have
failed. There is no 'return every NIN linked to a phone number' capability
on Techhub's side; the real phone-based lookup is the same tiered
'NIN by Phone' call already used by /nin's 'Phone No' method.

- Extracted the PHONE_TIERS/labels/icons/images/service-key mapping out
  of NinPhoneVerificationPage into shared.tsx (PHONE_TIER_*, PHONE_KEY)
  so both pages share one definition instead of drifting.
- Rewrote PhoneMultiplePage to call the real, working
  POST /verification/nin/by-phone endpoint with a tier, and added the
  Regular/Standard/Premium slip-type tiles (with the real branding
  photos), matching the reference design and NinPhoneVerificationPage's
  pattern. Removed the old results-array UI, which had no backend to
  ever populate it.
